{"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/DecisionDiagrams\/documentation\/DecisionDiagrams","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"metadata":{"role":"collection","modules":[{"name":"DecisionDiagrams"}],"roleHeading":"Framework","title":"DecisionDiagrams","externalID":"DecisionDiagrams","symbolKind":"module"},"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Canonical diagrams of Boolean functions and families of sets."}],"topicSections":[{"title":"Binary decision diagrams","identifiers":["doc:\/\/DecisionDiagrams\/documentation\/DecisionDiagrams\/BinaryDecisionDiagram"],"anchor":"Binary-decision-diagrams"},{"title":"Zero-suppressed decision diagrams","identifiers":["doc:\/\/DecisionDiagrams\/documentation\/DecisionDiagrams\/ZeroSuppressedDecisionDiagram"],"anchor":"Zero-suppressed-decision-diagrams"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/DecisionDiagrams\/documentation\/DecisionDiagrams\/BinaryDecisionDiagram"},{"type":"text","text":" is a table of reduced ordered binary decision diagrams (Bryant,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"1986). Each function is a directed acyclic graph whose vertices test variables in index order,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with a low child for the variable false and a high child for true, down to the constants. No two"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertices test the same variable with the same children, and none has equal children, so each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"function has exactly one root, and checking whether two functions are equal is comparing roots."}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["import DecisionDiagrams","","var diagram = BinaryDecisionDiagram(variableCount: 3)","let x0 = diagram.variable(0), x